00:12:12.898 --> 00:12:15.101
so we can just skip right over this in the future.

289
00:12:15.401 --> 00:12:16.969
And the description is really important.

290
00:12:17.369 --> 00:12:21.173
The intent of this user intent agent is to help the user

291
00:12:21.173 --> 00:12:23.876
ideate on knowledge graph use cases.

292
00:12:24.176 --> 00:12:27.179
This is helping the overall multi-agent system know

293
00:12:27.179 --> 00:12:28.881
when to use this agent itself.

294
00:12:29.081 --> 00:12:30.850
If you recall from the diagram

295
00:12:30.850 --> 00:12:32.885
earlier, this is part of a workflow

296
00:12:32.885 --> 00:12:35.488
by having this description match the role this agent

297
00:12:35.688 --> 00:12:37.790
plays within that workflow

298
00:12:37.790 --> 00:12:40.793
that helps the coordinator
that's going to be actually managing the workflow

299
00:12:40.793 --> 00:12:42.895
know when to delegate to this agent.

300
00:12:43.896 --> 00:12:47.166
Inside of the agent then,
we have the complete agent instructions

301
00:12:47.166 --> 00:12:49.869
that we assembled earlier. We're going to pass that in

302
00:12:49.869 --> 00:12:52.471
and of course, we'll also pass in the tools that are available.

303
00:12:55.574 --> 00:12:57.676
You now have a complete user agent

304
00:12:57.676 --> 00:12:59.779
ready to go. Let's interact with it.

